exports[`/privacy > renders the privacy page markup 1`] = `
"<div class="flex-1 bg-base-200 dark:bg-gradient-to-br dark:from-gray-950 dark:via-gray-900 dark:to-indigo-950">
<div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-3xl px-4 pt-6 pb-24 sm:pt-10 sm:pb-16">
<nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="breadcrumbs overflow-hidden text-sm text-base-content/70 dark:text-gray-400 py-0 mb-4">
<ol>
<li class="shrink-0">
<a class="link link-hover" href="/">Home</a>
</li>
<li class="min-w-0">
<span aria-current="page" class="min-w-0">
<span class="min-w-0 truncate">Privacy</span>
</span>
</li>
</ol>
</nav>
<article class="rounded-3xl border border-base-300 bg-base-100 p-5 sm:p-8 dark:border-white/10 dark:bg-gray-900/70">
<header class="mb-2">
<h1 class="m-0 mb-3 text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold leading-tight text-base-content">Privacy: what Tokenping stores and who handles it</h1>
<p class="m-0 text-sm text-base-content/70 dark:text-gray-400">Last updated <time dateTime="2026-10-14T00:00:00Z">14 October 2026</time>
</p>
</header>
<p class="my-4 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">This page describes what the app does today. Tokenping is in beta, and we update this page when what we collect changes.</p>
<h2 class="mt-10 mb-3 text-2xl font-bold leading-tight text-base-content">What you can do without giving us anything</h2>
<p class="my-4 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">Reading the site and the blog, and looking at your positions on the dashboard, adds nothing to our database. To show your positions, your browser asks RPC providers (listed below) for your wallet&#x27;s Aave data, so they see your wallet address.</p>
<h2 class="mt-10 mb-3 text-2xl font-bold leading-tight text-base-content">What we store when you save an alert</h2>
<ul class="my-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 marker:text-base-content/50 text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">
<li>Your wallet address.</li>
<li>The network the alert is for, and your threshold.</li>
<li>The channels you picked.</li>
<li>Your email address, if you chose email.</li>
<li>Your Signal username, if you chose Signal.</li>
<li>When the alert was created and last changed.</li>
</ul>
<p class="my-4 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">If you answer the optional &quot;How did you hear about Tokenping?&quot; question after saving an alert, we store your answer and the time with your wallet address.</p>
<h2 class="mt-10 mb-3 text-2xl font-bold leading-tight text-base-content">What we don&#x27;t store</h2>
<ul class="my-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 marker:text-base-content/50 text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">
<li>Your positions or a history of your health factor. They are read live and not saved.</li>
<li>A log of the alerts we sent.</li>
<li>Analytics, tracking pixels or advertising cookies: the site uses none, and Tokenping sets no cookies. Your browser keeps your theme choice, your wallet connection and whether it has already shown you the &quot;How did you hear about Tokenping?&quot; question in its own local storage.</li>
<li>IP addresses in our database. Vercel still handles every request, as listed below. When an alert check or a message fails, the error, which can include your wallet address and the recipient, goes to our server logs.</li>
</ul>
<h2 class="mt-10 mb-3 text-2xl font-bold leading-tight text-base-content">Who can see your alert settings</h2>
<p class="my-4 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">Alert settings are tied to a wallet address, not to an account with a password, and the app does not yet ask you to sign a message proving that you own the wallet.</p>
<p class="my-4 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">Until the app checks wallet signatures, anyone who knows your wallet address can look up the email address and Signal username saved for it and, while that wallet&#x27;s access is active, change or delete its alerts. The public payment records described below show which wallets have paid.</p>
<p class="my-4 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">Don&#x27;t enter an email address or Signal username you wouldn&#x27;t want linked to your wallet address.</p>
<h2 class="mt-10 mb-3 text-2xl font-bold leading-tight text-base-content">Who handles your data</h2>
<dl class="my-4 grid gap-3">
<div class="rounded-2xl border border-base-300 bg-base-200/60 p-4 dark:border-white/10 dark:bg-gray-900/40">
<dt class="font-semibold text-base-content">Vercel</dt>
<dd class="m-0 mt-1 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">Hosts this site and runs the alert check every 5 minutes.</dd>
<dd class="m-0 mt-1 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">Receives: Every request to the site, including your IP address, and our server logs.</dd>
</div>
<div class="rounded-2xl border border-base-300 bg-base-200/60 p-4 dark:border-white/10 dark:bg-gray-900/40">
<dt class="font-semibold text-base-content">Supabase</dt>
<dd class="m-0 mt-1 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">Our database.</dd>
<dd class="m-0 mt-1 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">Receives: The alert settings listed above.</dd>
</div>
<div class="rounded-2xl border border-base-300 bg-base-200/60 p-4 dark:border-white/10 dark:bg-gray-900/40">
<dt class="font-semibold text-base-content">Resend</dt>
<dd class="m-0 mt-1 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">Sends alert emails.</dd>
<dd class="m-0 mt-1 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">Receives: Your email address and the alert text.</dd>
</div>
<div class="rounded-2xl border border-base-300 bg-base-200/60 p-4 dark:border-white/10 dark:bg-gray-900/40">
<dt class="font-semibold text-base-content">Fly.io (our Signal relay)</dt>
<dd class="m-0 mt-1 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">Hosts the signal-cli-rest-api server we run, which hands Signal alerts to Signal.</dd>
<dd class="m-0 mt-1 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">Receives: Your Signal username and the alert text (and so does Signal).</dd>
</div>
<div class="rounded-2xl border border-base-300 bg-base-200/60 p-4 dark:border-white/10 dark:bg-gray-900/40">
<dt class="font-semibold text-base-content">RPC providers (PublicNode, Alchemy and the networks&#x27; public endpoints)</dt>
<dd class="m-0 mt-1 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">Answer the blockchain reads: from your browser for the dashboard, and from our server for alert checks.</dd>
<dd class="m-0 mt-1 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">Receives: The wallet address being read, and your IP address for reads made from your browser.</dd>
</div>
<div class="rounded-2xl border border-base-300 bg-base-200/60 p-4 dark:border-white/10 dark:bg-gray-900/40">
<dt class="font-semibold text-base-content">WalletConnect</dt>
<dd class="m-0 mt-1 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">Relays the connection between this site and your wallet app, if you connect with WalletConnect.</dd>
<dd class="m-0 mt-1 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">Receives: What your wallet app and this site exchange to connect, such as your wallet address.</dd>
</div>
</dl>
<p class="my-4 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">Each of these services handles that data under its own privacy policy.</p>
<h2 class="mt-10 mb-3 text-2xl font-bold leading-tight text-base-content">What is public on the blockchain</h2>
<p class="my-4 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">Paying for alerts happens on Arbitrum One. Each payment records the paying address, the token, the amount, the time, the period bought and the new expiry date in a public event that anyone can read and nobody can delete. Your alert settings are never written to a blockchain.</p>
<h2 class="mt-10 mb-3 text-2xl font-bold leading-tight text-base-content">How long we keep it, and how to delete it</h2>
<ul class="my-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 marker:text-base-content/50 text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">
<li>Alert settings stay until you delete the alert in the dashboard. Deleting removes that network&#x27;s settings, including the email address and Signal username, and needs active access.</li>
<li>If your access has expired, or you want your &quot;How did you hear about Tokenping?&quot; answer removed, message us on<!-- --> <a href="https://x.com/tokenping" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="link underline-offset-2 text-indigo-700 hover:text-indigo-900 dark:text-indigo-300 dark:hover:text-indigo-200">X</a> <!-- -->or in our<!-- --> <a href="https://t.me/tokenping_xyz" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="link underline-offset-2 text-indigo-700 hover:text-indigo-900 dark:text-indigo-300 dark:hover:text-indigo-200">Telegram community</a> <!-- -->and we&#x27;ll delete it.</li>
<li>Payments on the blockchain can&#x27;t be deleted by anyone.</li>
</ul>
<p class="my-4 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">Questions about how alerts work are answered on the<!-- --> <a class="link underline-offset-2 text-indigo-700 hover:text-indigo-900 dark:text-indigo-300 dark:hover:text-indigo-200" href="/">homepage</a>.</p>
</article>
<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://tokenping.xyz/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Privacy"}]}</script>
</div>
</div>"
`;
